    "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting": {
      "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting",
      "type": "line",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l0",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "Iona has found time to put the clean glasses away. She looks up when you come to the bar.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:14"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l1",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "There you are. I have both my things back and the glasses are washed. Thank you for all that. / That looks familiar. Bring it over; there is room on the bar. / No hurry about that thing of mine. I just thought I ought to ask while there is still someone going in. / You have already helped with the glasses. You do not owe me another errand. Ask again if you change your mind. / You saved me two trips at exactly the right moment. Could I ask you about something else?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:15"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l2",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "There you are. Bring those over. Mind the dominoes if Bert has tried to clear them onto the tray.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:20"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l3",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Thank you for taking those over. Bert and Farah have the empty glasses, at the next table. Then bring the tray back here.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:21"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l4",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Mavis and Ed, nearest the entrance. Bus badge and work jacket. Those two waters are theirs.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:22"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l5",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "The tray is on the public side of the counter. Two waters to Mavis and Ed, then the empties from the domino table.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:23"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l6",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "The bartender sets down a glass, hears her name from the snug, and picks it up again.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:25"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l7",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Evening. Iona Reed. I would come out and say hello properly, but I have been about to do that for twenty minutes.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:26"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.greeting.l8",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Could you give me a hand for a minute? Two waters to take over, a few glasses to bring back. Only if you have the time.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:27"
        }
      ],
      "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:14"
    },
    "buildPubBartenderDialogue": {
      "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue",
      "type": "choice",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l0",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "I lent my bottle opener to the conservatory staff kitchen. They had a leaving do. I got the tray back and a very sincere thank-you, but not the opener.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:85"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l1",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "It is the flat steel one with LYRIC stamped by the hole. If you are in the staff kitchen, could you bring it back to me? No need to make a special trip.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:86"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l2",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "The box office borrowed our order book for the last reception. They were counting the drinks out of it. Brown cover, red cloth on the spine.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:88"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l3",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "It should still be in the front-of-house box office. My father’s old supplier numbers are in the back. Would you bring it over if you come across it?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:89"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l4",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Thank you. The staff kitchen. You will know it by the name stamped into it. / Thank you. Front of house, in the box office. The numbers in the back are probably all wrong now, but I would like them back anyway.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:91"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l5",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "All right. If you happen to have time later, ask me again.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:92"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l6",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "The flat steel bottle opener, LYRIC by the hole / The brown order book with the red cloth spine. {spec.location.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + spec.location.slice(1)}. Bring it back here when you have it.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:93"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l7",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "Iona tests the opener in her palm and hangs it from a hook under the bar.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:95"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l8",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "That is the one. I had got used to reaching for it and finding the nail. Thank you.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:96"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l9",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "Iona opens the book from the back. Her thumb stops beside a pencilled telephone number.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:98"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l10",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "There. I knew I had not imagined that handwriting.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:99"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l11",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Thank you. For doing all that. Nobody made it your job.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:100"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l12",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Then somebody knew while other people were still being asked whether they had seen him. / The ringing room. People used to come in with the rope marks still on their hands.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:118"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l13",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "I can keep a room warm. I cannot put right what they did across the road by putting a signature on a petition.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:121"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l14",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "They asked for acknowledgment before another rehearsal. Was that too much to ask?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:131"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l15",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "No. I would have wanted it written down. I would not tell somebody to sit at a piano first.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:132"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l16",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Some stopped eating as well. You can take a plate upstairs. You cannot make someone accept it.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:133"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l17",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "What are the people outside trying to save?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:136"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l18",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Their lessons. A view from a window. Somewhere they used to go with somebody. You would get a different answer from each chair.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:137"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l19",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Keeping a room and asking people to start playing in it again are different requests. The petition puts them on the same sheet.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:138"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l20",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "A room, a window, a chair. It is a comfortable list to despise. I can keep doing that without deciding what I owe anyone inside.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:139"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l21",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "I keep making this about their comforts. The students were asking for something else.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:143"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l22",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Then ask for that. You do not have to sign the rest.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:144"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l23",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "Yes. Separate questions. I can be very precise about separate questions while the four hundred pounds stays one sum.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:145"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l24",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "Would bringing it down help the people who are still there?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:148"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l25",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "I do not know. I would like somebody who says they know to tell me how they found out.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:149"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l26",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "And I would like whoever wants another concert to ask the people who already said no.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:150"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l27",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "What happens to the pub if Ellery comes down?",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:153"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l28",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "Fewer people one month. Builders the next, perhaps. New neighbours after that, if anything gets built. Nobody has promised me the order.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:154"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l29",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "I have wages on Friday whichever version wins. That is why I ask about Friday. It is not the only day I know exists.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:155"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l30",
          "who": "me",
          "text": "People died in there. This cannot just be about keeping the bar open.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:158"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l31",
          "who": "unknown",
          "text": "I did not say it was. There are people who need somewhere warm tonight as well.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:159"
        },
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.l32",
          "who": "direction",
          "text": "A practical answer. I like practical answers. Mine is that I am only here to do a job.",
          "source": "src/data/pub-dialogue.js:160"
        }
      ],
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "buildPubBartenderDialogue.c0",
